prompt:
Source-only Lobo comprehension. No tools, execution, editing or delegation.
READING MODE: reason from the supplied source and return the requested JSON without tools.
Lobo 1.11.2 is a native language. There is no projection/interpreter step.
Each block returns its final expression without a trailing semicolon. Use fn f(x:I64)->I64 {x+1}, let x=...; if condition {a} else {b}, &&/||/!, checked I64 arithmetic, and ==/!= comparisons. Names cannot shadow other visible names or function/type declarations. No assignment, break, continue, return keyword or for statement.
Records: record Pair {left:I64,right:I64}; Pair {left:1,right:2}; pair.left; Pair {...pair,left:3}. Variants: match event {Credit(n)=> expression,Debit(n)=> expression,Lock=> expression,Unlock=> expression}. Every case must occur. Expected types infer case owners. Parenthesize complex match subjects: match (cursor.best) {...}.
Lists: List<T>, List::empty<I64>(), List::prepend(value,list), List::length(list), List::head(list), List::tail(list). Head/tail require nonempty. Prepend reverses order; the supplied util.reverse<T> restores order and may infer T. Lists are persistent; no indexing, append or mutation operation.
Counted loops carry one typed value: fold(i in n,total:I64=0) {total+i}. The index runs 0..n-1; zero iterations return the initial state. For multiple variables, carry a record: fold(i in List::length(items),state:Cursor=Cursor {pending:items,total:0}) {Cursor {pending:List::tail(state.pending),total:state.total+List::head(state.pending)}}. State-driven loop: while(state:State=initial; condition_using_state) {new_state}. To stop early, carry a Bool and test it in the loop condition. Finite execution fuel/heap apply; do not use deep recursive traversal.
Bytes: Bytes::length(data), Bytes::at(data,index) returns 0..255, Bytes::slice(data,start,count), Bytes::empty(), Bytes::push(data,value). Guard bounds before at/slice. List<Bytes> is supported. Remainder uses %, division truncates toward zero. Ordinary expected failures are values in the declared DTO, not runtime faults.

The host supplies correct stable identity metadata. RESPONSE CONTRACT v2. Return exactly one JSON object, without Markdown. All objects in this profile are closed: every required field must occur, unknown fields and duplicate keys are invalid. Integers use integer tokens, never 1.0 or true. Put any explanation in the optional top-level notes string. Shape validity and semantic correctness are separate checks. Input domain bounds in the task still apply.
{"additional_properties": false, "kind": "object", "optional": {"notes": {"kind": "string"}}, "required": {"admissions": {"items": {"kind": "boolean"}, "kind": "array", "length": 4}, "predictions": {"items": {"kind": "integer", "rule": "JSON integer token, not float or boolean"}, "kind": "array", "length": 6}}}

Predict I64 results of p0..p5 in order as six JSON integers. Classify four admission fragments as static-check acceptance booleans, not runtime success or contract proof. Keep shared types/helpers, remove p0..p5, and append each fragment independently. No fragment sees another. No extra input values are required.
PROGRAM:
module compact;
fn add(value:I64)->I64 requires {value>=0} ensures {result>value} {value+5}
fn post(value:I64)->I64 ensures {result==value*2} {value*2}
fn p0()->I64 {add(8)}
fn p1()->I64 {if false {add(-7)} else {27}}
fn p2()->I64 {if true || add(-1)>0 {17} else {0}}
fn p3()->I64 {fold(i in 0,total:I64=12) {add(-9)}}
fn p4()->I64 {post(9)}
fn p5()->I64 {if false && 1/0==0 {1} else {29}}

ADMISSION FRAGMENTS:
CASE 0
fn candidate()->I64 ensures {result<0} {14}
CASE 1
fn candidate()->I64 ensures {result+1} {9}
CASE 2
fn observe()->I64 actions {pilot.audit} {3} fn candidate()->I64 actions {pilot.audit} ensures {true || observe()>0} {1}
CASE 3
fn candidate()->I64 requires {false} {if false {1/0} else {2}}
Return only the requested JSON object.

CHECKED TOPIC CARD: Lobo 1.11.2 / Core 1.11
requires and ensures expressions must be Bool and pure, regardless of the enclosing function action declaration. Calls to any function with a nonempty DECLARED action bound are forbidden in contracts, even if its body is currently pure or its call is in an unreachable/short-circuited branch. All functions, branches and generic bodies are statically checked, including unused ones. Static checking establishes types/actions, not truth of preconditions/postconditions, termination or absence of runtime faults. A well-typed false contract or unexecuted faulting expression can pass check. On invocation, preconditions run before the body; postconditions run after normal or propagated results. Short-circuiting skips unevaluated calls at runtime only.
